# The app

Action: $ARGUMENTS (default: start the `app`)

| App | Start | URL | Stop |
|---|---|---|---|
| `app` | `uv run {{ project_name }} app` | http://localhost:{{ app_port }} | `pkill -f "streamlit run .*/{{ package }}/app/main.py"` |
{%- for a in extra_apps %}
| `{{ a.name }}` | `uv run {{ project_name }} app {{ a.name }}` | http://localhost:{{ a.port }} | `pkill -f "streamlit run .*/{{ package }}/{{ a.name }}/main.py"` |
{%- endfor %}

Health: `curl -s localhost:<port>/_stcore/health` → `ok`. Do not use `pkill -f streamlit` alone: it stops other apps.

## Start

1. Send a request to the health URL. If the answer is `ok`, give the link to the user. Stop here.
2. Start the app in the background. It runs until you stop it.
3. Send requests to the health URL until the answer is `ok`, then give the link.

The app listens only on localhost. It does not open a browser tab.

## Restart

After a code change: stop the app, then start it.
{%- if tailnet %}

## Tailnet

Use the tailnet when the arguments contain `tailnet`, or when the user wants the app on another device.

1. Start the app with `--tailnet` added. The command prints a URL: give it to the user.
2. The app still listens only on localhost. `tailscale serve` forwards `https://<this machine's tailnet name>:<port>`
   to it. Only devices on the user's tailnet can open it. The forward stops when the app stops.
3. The first time, Tailscale can print a link that turns on Serve (HTTPS) for the tailnet. Only the user can open it.
4. If Tailscale is not found or not connected, the app does not start. Ask the user to connect Tailscale.

Do not use `tailscale funnel`. It puts the app on the public internet.
{%- endif %}
{%- if demo_data %}

## Demo

With `demo`, add `--demo`: the app reads `data/demo.duckdb` (synthetic data), safe for screenshots.
{%- endif %}

## Data

The app reads a snapshot of the contract views; it does not block `ingest`.
- After an ingest, tell the user to click *Reload data*.
- If the app says that the database does not match the contract, run `uv run {{ project_name }} ingest`.
